# VIII04 — the non-extremal RN background on the whole exterior `I = (R_h, ∞)`

`R` is the **squared** radial variable of the frozen VI/paper gauge (Fröb et al. 2022, radial gauge
of Eqs. 23–25). For real `R_h > R_i ≥ 0` and `Q² = 3 R_h R_i / 4` put

* `n1 = -(R_h + R_i)`, `n0 = R_h R_i` (`= 4Q²/3`),
* `N0(R) = (R - R_h)(R - R_i) = R² + n1 R + n0`, `f0 = N0/R²`, `m0 = N0/R`, `p0 = Q/R`, `a0 = w0 = 0`,
* `P = N0/R` and `V = 1/R + 4Q²/R³` (coefficients of the magnetic operator, used in `Linearize`).

`R_h` is the outer root of `N0` in the squared variable, not an areal radius and not a mass.
